---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('tare')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 23, 2026';
const sections = [
  { href: '#availability', label: 'Availability' },
  { href: '#identity', label: 'Accounts and identity' },
  { href: '#health-cloud', label: 'Health and iCloud' },
  { href: '#ai', label: 'Optional AI' },
  { href: '#backup', label: 'Backup and restore' },
  { href: '#deletion', label: 'Deletion and retired web data' },
  { href: '#troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { href: '#contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  app={app}
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with Tare for iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch, including HealthKit, private CloudKit, optional AI, backups, offline use, and retired web data."
  path="/tare/support"
  page="support"
  heading="Tare Support"
  documentMeta={`Updated ${updatedDate} · iOS 17+ · watchOS 10+`}
  summary="Tare 1.0 (31) is a native-only internal TestFlight build for iPhone, iPad, and Apple Watch. It has no Tare account, no web login, and no public App Store listing."
  sections={sections}
  evidenceNote="Support guidance was reviewed against immutable Tare-for-iOS release-visual authority 9154a7e, the matching relay-only deployment, and active retirement gates on August 23, 2026."
>
  <section id="availability" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Current availability</h2>
    <p class="legal-callout">
      Tare 1.0 (31) is VALID, attached to an editable App Store version, and
      assigned only to internal TestFlight. It supports iPhone and iPad on iOS 17
      or later, with an Apple Watch companion on watchOS 10 or later. There is no
      public TestFlight acquisition link, public App Store listing, authorized
      price, or territory claim.
    </p>
    <p>
      The retired web address shows retirement information only. It is not a
      supported Tare web app, sign-in page, export portal, or route to the native
      health store.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="identity" class="legal-section">
    <h2>No Tare account or web sign-in</h2>
    <p>
      Native Tare opens without an account. Your Apple Account may provide private
      CloudKit sync and Apple Health may provide approved records, but neither is
      a Nintek-managed Tare account. Support will never ask for an Apple password,
      verification code, App Attest token, or iCloud credential.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="health-cloud" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Troubleshoot Apple Health and private iCloud</h2>
    <h3>Apple Health</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Review Tare’s Health permissions in Apple Settings or the Health app.</li>
      <li>
        Open Tare or return it to the foreground after enabling access, then use
        <strong>Sync now</strong> if you need an immediate check.
      </li>
      <li>
        Weight, glucose, and dietary water can sync both ways; sleep and steps
        are read only. Manually entered weight and glucose values take
        precedence over imports. Water is the exception — Tare re-totals the
        day’s figure from Health after writing to it, so it does not preserve
        an entered override.
      </li>
      <li>
        Apple Health authorization is a system control. Reinstalling Tare does not
        guarantee that Apple will present the same permission prompt again.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Private CloudKit</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm the device is signed in to the intended Apple Account.</li>
      <li>Check iCloud availability, network access, and free iCloud storage.</li>
      <li>Open Tare on each device and allow Apple time to deliver changes.</li>
      <li>
        Do not delete the app while troubleshooting if a device may contain the
        only local copy of records you need.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nintek cannot inspect, merge, force, or restore a private CloudKit database.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ai" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Troubleshoot optional AI features</h2>
    <p>
      AI is off until you accept the current consent scope. Confirm AI is enabled
      under Tare’s privacy settings, the device is online, and the selected input
      is within the feature’s stated scope. A changed scope asks for consent again.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a request fails, retry once after reconnecting. The relay keeps no request
      or answer database, so support cannot retrieve a failed transcript. Report
      the feature name, time, app build, and visible error without sending a full
      health database, medication history, or unredacted lab document.
    </p>
    <p>
      Generated output can be wrong and is not medical advice. Do not use it to
      choose a medication, dose, diagnosis, or treatment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Anthropic processes the scoped input as the processor behind these
      features, under its own
      <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/commercial-terms">Commercial Terms of Service</a>.
      See the <a href="/tare/privacy#ai">Tare Privacy Policy</a> for the full
      data-handling and retention detail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="backup" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Backup, restore, export, and offline limits</h2>
    <p>
      Tare exports a JSON backup containing all 16 data tables and can restore a
      compatible native or former web backup. It keeps one rolling local backup
      per day for 14 days and attempts a separate safety copy before every restore.
      Keep an independent copy before a device migration or destructive
      troubleshooting step. The file contains health information; store and share
      it accordingly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Core records remain usable offline. CloudKit, Health delivery between
      services, and optional AI wait for the required Apple or internet service.
      Nintek does not hold a native server backup and cannot recreate a lost local
      store from the relay.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="deletion" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Deletion and the retained legacy web database</h2>
    <p>
      There is no native Tare account to delete. Deleting the app removes its local
      data from that device, but private CloudKit data, Apple Health records, and
      exported backup files have separate controls. Tare has no in-app erase-all
      control.
    </p>
    <p>
      The former web database is separate and has not yet been destructively
      removed. Cleanup is waiting for physical-device validation, completion and
      review of the active soak, native-successor acceptance, and explicit
      confirmation. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a> about
      access to or deletion of a retained legacy copy. Do not use obsolete web
      login instructions; the web product is retired.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="legal-section">
    <h2>General troubleshooting</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm the device meets the iOS, iPadOS, or watchOS requirement.</li>
      <li>Install the newest private build available to the authorized Apple Account.</li>
      <li>Force-quit and reopen Tare, then restart the device if needed.</li>
      <li>Check free device storage before importing or creating a backup.</li>
      <li>
        For Apple Watch delivery, keep Bluetooth and Wi-Fi available, open Tare on
        the iPhone, and allow queued entries time to transfer.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Avoid deleting Tare as an early recovery step when the device may hold the
      only local copy of important records.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Contact and legal documents</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the
      device model, operating-system version, Tare build, affected feature, and
      recovery steps already tried. Do not send credentials or more health data
      than the issue requires.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/tare/privacy">Tare Privacy Policy</a> for data locations,
      providers, retention, and deletion boundaries. Use of Tare is subject to the
      <a href="/terms">Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
